<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/2nd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Han–Xiongnu War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">from 129 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Han–<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a> War was a long series of conflicts between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a> and the Xiongnu confederation, entering its offensive phase from 129 BCE under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wu-of-han">Emperor Wu</a>. Han armies campaigned deep into the steppe and secured the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gansu-corridor">Hexi Corridor</a>. The war reshaped the northern frontier and opened routes to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>, though at great financial cost to the Han.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/han-xiongnu-war.jpg" alt="Han–Xiongnu War" width="320" height="233" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PHG · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ZhangQianTravels.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
